finalText:
Found it. Problem in engine.js lines 24-27.

Implementation rounds after each coupon, but test's reference only rounds once at end. Double rounding on stacked coupons causes drift:

```javascript
// WRONG (current)
if (percent) {
  usd = round(usd * (1 - percent.amount), 2);
}
if (flat) {
  usd = round(usd - flat.amountUsd, 2);  // <-- rounding error compounds
}
```

```javascript
// RIGHT (reference)
if (percent) usd = usd * (1 - percent.amount);
if (flat) usd = usd - flat.amountUsd;
// round only once after convert
```

Example: $19.98 with 10% off then -$5:
- Wrong path: 19.98 * 0.9 = 17.982 → rounds to 17.98 → 17.98 - 5 = 12.98
- Right path: 19.98 * 0.9 = 17.982 → 17.982 - 5 = 12.982 → rounds to 12.98 (might differ in conversion)

Multiply by currency rates and multiple orders — cents add up. Fix: remove lines 24 and 27's `round()` calls.
